endobj
168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (The scope of the internship covered the complete beginner-to-intermediate AI development pipeline over four structured weeks: \(1\) Python foundations and data handling; \(2\) classical machine learning with supervised learning algorithms; \(3\) neural networks and deep learning, including CNNs for image data; and \(4\) advanced applications in NLP and Reinforcement Learning, concluding with a capstone project. Within this scope, the practical, hands-on component of the internship focused specifically on two applied machine learning projects built end-to-end: a Handwritten Digit Recognizer \(an image classification task using neural networks, connecting to the Week 3 deep learning/CNN module\) and a Spam Message Classifier \(a text classification task using Natural Language Processing techniques, connecting to the Week 4 NLP module\). These two projects together cover both major branches of applied AI explored during the internship - vision-based classification and text-based classification - and served as the practical demonstration of concepts learned across all four weeks.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
169 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (The scope did not extend to production-grade deployment \(e.g., hosting the models as live web services with continuous training pipelines\), as the internship's focus was on building strong conceptual and practical foundations within the one-month duration.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
