<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (Both practical projects developed during the internship follow a standard supervised machine learning pipeline, which can be summarized as: Data Input -> Data Preprocessing -> Feature Extraction -> Model Training -> Model Evaluation -> Prediction/Output. Figure 4.1 illustrates this general architecture as applied to the two projects.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
199 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (For the Handwritten Digit Recognizer: raw pixel data of 8x8 grayscale digit images is first scaled using a StandardScaler, then fed into a Multi-Layer Perceptron \(MLP\) neural network with two hidden layers \(64 and 32 neurons, ReLU activation\), which outputs a predicted digit class \(0-9\).)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
200 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (For the Spam Message Classifier: raw text messages are converted into numerical TF- IDF \(Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency\) feature vectors after stop-word removal, which are then passed to a Multinomial Naive Bayes classifier that outputs a predicted label \("spam" or "ham"\).)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
